From 9f04cd2a20f8c89525a84e5031b8007321514b43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:56:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] requeued publisher: an earlier PR needs a recorded
 handoff to the requeued claim; probe schema once; skip the scan with no
 requeue

Follow-up to PR #1818 review nits (review 5885076095, card t_01a1d2b3476ab649).

1. continues() assumed holding PR comments from before the requeued run's claim
   were cleared by the respawn guard. A direct claim_task bypasses the guard, so
   an earlier crashed publisher's PR rode along once the claimed run restated it
   and was requeued. Now fail closed: such an earlier PR needs a handoff event
   (the kinds the guard honours, re-validated: owner dependency park, reopen of
   a done card, one-continuation hold release / operator resume, real reassign,
   unblock, continued, scheduled, changes_requested, review_reopened) after the
   comment, after every earlier real run ended, and no later than the claim.
   Core-update requeues and unused grants between do not consume it. A PR from
   before the card's first run is a handoff's input. Unreadable run starts/ends
   hold.
2. The task_runs.uid schema probe runs once per continues() call, not per comment.
3. Cheap pre-check: no core-update requeue on the card (requeued_run_ids) returns
   False before get_task or the commented-event scan.

Proof:
- RED on origin/main: 13 of the new tests fail; GREEN: 29 files importing
  kanban_requeued_publisher / kanban_core_update_requeue / kanban_db_dispatch_pr_state,
  634 passed.
- Mutants: 18 of 18 new/changed conditions killed (sdlc-review mutants.py).
- Replay (read-only) of active_pr_reason old vs new continues() over the 161 real
  cards with a core-update reclaim on hermes-worker-1's board: 0 verdict changes.
